        // C(n, m) * 2^m * sum_{i=0}^{n - m} C(n - m, i) (-2)^i * (m + i)!^2 / (2(m + i) + 1)!.

        // This seems computationally feasible for n up to 2000.

        // Let's compute this for each m from k to n and sum them up.

